WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.060
How are the slopes of two parallel lines related?

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.180
Take these two parallel lines for example.

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.860
If the slope of this line is M1

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.480
and that of this one is M2,

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:19.100
then how are M1 and M2 related?

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.020
You don't really have to think here.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.520
It's obvious.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.440
The tilt or the inclination is the same.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.800
M1 will be equal to M2.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.260
The slopes of parallel lines are the same.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.620
Okay, great!

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.520
So how are the slopes of two lines

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.640
that are perpendicular to each other related?

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.920
Take these two lines for instance.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.600
Assume their slopes are 'M3 'and 'M4'.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.680
This may not be obvious,

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.180
but the product of their slopes is 'minus 1'.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:54.280
'M3' times 'M4' is equal to 'minus 1'.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.320
Another fancy way to say it

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.400
would be that they are negative reciprocals of each other.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.980
'M3' will equal 'minus 1' over 'M4'.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:08.220
And 'M4' will equal 'minus 1' over 'M3'.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:12.000
If lines are parallel, their slopes are equal.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.080
And if they are perpendicular,

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:17.940
then the product of their slopes is 'minus 1'.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:23.520
In this example, we are given the coordinates of A and B

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.100
and have been asked to find the equation of the

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:29.420
perpendicular bisector of 'AB'.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.700
Pause the video and try finding the equation.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:44.640
First, let's plot the two points on the coordinate plane.

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:47.200
'3' comma 'minus 1' will be here.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:50.740
And '1' comma '3' will be this point.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:53.440
Let's join points A and B.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:57.520
It's perpendicular bisector will look a bit like this.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:59.340
Let's call it 'CD'.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:05.040
'CD' is perpendicular to 'AB' and it will also bisect 'AB'.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.760
Now we've been asked to find the equation of this blue line,

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.780
the equation of line 'CD'.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:13.780
With the slope intercept form,

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:18.620
let's assume that it's equation is 'Y is equal to MX plus B'.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.820
How do we find the equation?

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:23.320
We need 'M' and 'B'.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.340
'M' is the slope of 'CD'.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:28.100
And 'B' is its 'Y' intercept.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:31.020
How can we find the slope of 'CD'?

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.140
To find the slope of any line,

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:37.360
we need the coordinates of at least two of its points.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:39.980
We have the coordinates of A and B.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.780
Which can give us the slope of 'AB'.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.660
And as 'AB' and 'CD' are perpendicular,

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:49.760
the slope of 'AB' will give us the slope of 'CD'.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.660
Their product will equal 'minus one'.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.160
So we will have 'M'.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:59.280
Now how do we find 'B', which is the 'Y' intercept?

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:01.600
Look at the slope-intercept form.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.140
If we have 'M',

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:07.940
then we just need the coordinates of one point on CD to find B.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.300
Because then,

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:14.460
we can substitute the coordinates in place of 'X' and 'Y' and get 'B'.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:18.620
The only point at which we can find the coordinates is this one.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.860
The intersection of 'AB' and 'CD'.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:25.460
Because it is also a midpoint of 'AB'.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.200
And we can easily find the midpoint of 'AB'

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:31.540
as we have the coordinates of its endpoints.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:34.240
So after we get the slope of 'CD',

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.400
we find the midpoint of 'AB',

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.220
which will also give us 'B'.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.420
Once we have 'M' and 'B',

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:44.480
we can easily find the equation of 'CD'.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:47.860
Okay, so what is the slope of 'AB'?

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.520
It will be 'minus 1', 'minus 3', over '3 minus 1'.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:57.880
Difference of Y coordinates over the difference of X coordinates.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:59.880
This gives us 'minus 2'.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:03.700
The slope of 'AB' is 'minus 2'.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:06.140
Now we find the slope of 'CD'.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:09.000
As 'AB' and 'CD' are perpendicular,

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:12.320
the product of the slopes will be 'minus 1'.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:16.820
So 'minus 2' times 'M' will equal 'minus 1'.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:22.260
Slope of 'AB' times the slope of 'CD' equals 'minus 1'.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:26.200
We get the slope of 'CD' as 1 over 2.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:28.960
Now we get to the midpoint of AB.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:31.220
The X coordinate of the midpoint

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:35.260
is the average of the X coordinates of the endpoints.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:39.880
The X coordinate will be 3 plus 1 over 2.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.160
And the Y coordinate of the midpoint,

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:46.060
will be 'minus 1 plus 3 over 2'.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:49.040
2 comma 1 will be the midpoint of 'AB'.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:52.120
And it is also one of the points on 'CD'.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:56.660
So we can substitute these values in place of X and Y.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:05:00.300
Substituting the values of M, X and Y here,

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:04.800
we get 'one equals half times two plus B'.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:08.860
Solving this we get the value of  'B as zero'.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:12.140
'M is half' and 'B is zero'.

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:18.020
The equation of line 'CD' will be 'Y is equal to X over 2'.

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:21.180
This video, was a bit taxing I'm sure.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.440
If you haven't understood it well,

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:25.840
make sure you go through it again.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.740
I am sure, it will make more sense.

